@startuml chooser_flow
title paddock: the chooser, one form in and one plan out

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

start
:herdr popup runs `paddock`\n(no subcommand means `choose`);

if (subcommand) then (profiles)
  :print one line per profile:\nagent, workdir, network;
  stop
elseif (launch <profile>) then
  :load the saved profile\n(--cwd shares that directory instead);
  :plan = NewSession(profile);
elseif (attach <session>) then
  :plan = Attach(session ref, cwd only if --cwd was given);
else (choose)
  :sessions.list_sessions();
  partition "the form: one screen, one field per decision" {
    repeat
      :the fields, filled in from the profile\nthis workspace launched last:\n1 Open: a new sandbox, a local tab, or a live session\n2 Profile: fills in everything below\n3 Backend: srt now, or msb when this machine has one\n4 Agent: the command, and the key it is saved under\n5 Tools: ticked binaries on the sandbox PATH\n6 Network: groups, and any extra domains\n7 Files: an isolated scratch dir, or one shared directory\n8 Skills: from the agent's own config dir\n9 Advanced: the name, saving these answers, keeping\nthe session running, MCP, writes, reads, the system PATH;
      :enter opens an editor for that field,\nesc closes it and keeps what it holds;
      :settle(answers, field) after a change:\nanother profile hands over every value it carries,\nanother agent drops its skills and typed command,\nsharing nothing drops the directory;
    repeat while (another field?) is (yes: the arrows or a digit,\nevery answer kept) not (no: Launch)
  }
  if (what the Open field says) then (Local tab)
    :plan = Local(cwd);
  elseif (Attach: <session>) then
    :plan = Attach(session id):\nthe session keeps its own workdir;
  else (New sandbox)
    partition "confirm" {
      repeat
        :the resolved policy, in full: session name, agent,\nthe profile and whether the answers still match it,\ncan write, can read, can reach (the domains the\ngroups open, not the group names), can run, can see;
      repeat while (Launch, Back to the form, or Cancel?) is (Back to the form:\nthe same screen, every answer kept) not (Launch)
    }
    :plan = NewSession(profile, name, save as);
  endif
endif

if (--dry-run) then (yes)
  :print what would happen;
  stop
else (no)
endif

:save the profile and remember a typed-in\nagent, if the answers asked for it;
:screen.progress("Starting <name>"):\nthe image it pulls, the agent it installs in the guest,\nand the warning when the profile cannot reach npm;
:sessions.launch_local\n| get_session then attach\n| launch;
if (did it open a pane?) then (yes)
  :print the pane id;
  stop
else (no: it raised)
  :screen.failed(the message, the log path):\nBack to the form reopens it with answers_from(plan),\nCancel closes the popup;
  stop
endif

note right
  Ctrl-C cancels at any depth, and Cancel on the
  confirm says the same thing: the chooser returns
  no plan and cli.py stops. Only cli.py acts on a
  plan; the chooser reads the session list and
  nothing else. So backing out cannot leave a pane
  or a file behind.

  Esc backs out one level and never loses an answer.
  It closes what is open, keeps the value it was
  editing, and puts the cursor back on the field.
  There is no walk to go back through, because every
  field is on one screen.

  Picking a local tab or a session greys out every
  field below Open: no sandbox, so there is nothing
  to permit. Nothing is hidden and nothing moves. A
  session that ended between the list and the form
  says so, rather than reading as a new sandbox.

  Nothing the popup was asked to do dies without a
  screen. The popup closes with the process, so a
  message printed after the form has gone is written
  to a terminal nobody is left looking at: a launch
  that never opened a pane is drawn instead, and Back
  to the form keeps every answer behind it.

  tui.py holds the fields, the words and the rules;
  screen.py draws them (chooser_keys.puml), and
  recent.py is what the form opens on.
end note

@enduml
